ignores the loopback port, but not the path). Works with **Allow public client flows** disabled, and is unaffected by Conditional Access policies that block device-code authentication.\n"+"- **`broker`** \u2014 signs in through the OS identity broker (Web Account Manager on Windows, Company Portal on macOS), so it can satisfy Conditional Access policies that require a compliant/managed device or token protection. The app registration must include the broker redirect URIs `ms-appx-web://Microsoft.AAD.BrokerPlugin/{client-id}` (Windows) and `msauth.com.anthropic.claudefordesktop://auth` (macOS) under the **Mobile and desktop applications** platform. Not supported on Linux.\n\n"+"App versions that predate this key always use device code; versions that predate the broker option treat `broker` as unset and use device code.")}})}),W$.HelperScriptCreds]),Dee=x.z.object({provider:x.z.literal("foundry"),resource:T.field(see.optional(),{flatKey:"inferenceFoundryResource",readers:["desktop","m365"],support:{enabled:{scopes:["3p"],availableInVersion:"1.2581.0"}},title:R.msg({defaultMessage:"Azure AI Foundry resource name",id:"tdj4b/xhUV"}),egressRequirements:(e,t)=>{var r;return((r=t.inference)===null||r===void 0?void 0:r.provider)==="foundry"&&e?[`${e}.services.ai.azure.com`]:[]},category:"connection",predicates:{required:(e)=>!Pe.hasActiveBootstrap(e)},placeholder:R.msg({defaultMessage:"my-foundry-resource",id:"CWxAZo6MyF"}),description:{short:T.shortDescription(R.msg({defaultMessage:"Azure AI Foundry resource name used to construct the endpoint URL.",id:"XfOmm8BNBA"}))}}),...Xs,credential:Ree.optional()});W$.InferenceConfig=x.z.discriminatedUnion("provider",[T.variantMeta(Oee,{}),T.variantMeta(Eee,{noBearerFor:["interactive"]}),T.variantMeta(Iee,{cliFlag:"CLAUDE_CODE_USE_BEDROCK",bedrockFamily:!0,noDiscoveryFor:["interactive","vendor-profile"],noBearerFor:["interactive","vendor-profile"]}),T.variantMeta(Aee,{cliFlag:"CLAUDE_CODE_USE_MANTLE",bedrockFamily:!0,noDiscoveryFor:["