e app does to its gateway or bootstrap server (url).",id:"mktCredKd3"}))}},ZA={expectedName:ae.subfield(et.z.string().regex(/^[A-Za-z0-9](?:[A-Za-z0-9._-]{0,126}[A-Za-z0-9_-])?$/,"Expected name must start with a letter or number, may contain only letters, numbers, dots, underscores, and hyphens, and must not end with a dot (128 characters max)").optional(),{label:pe.msg({defaultMessage:"Expected name",id:"pMktExpNm1"}),description:{short:ae.shortDescription(pe.msg({defaultMessage:"Rejects the marketplace if its manifest name differs.",id:"pMktExpNm3"}),{docsOnly:!1}),long:ae.longDescription("When set, each fetch or clone is rejected if the marketplace's `manifest.name` differs, so an upstream rename cannot silently replace another configured marketplace.",{docsOnly:!1})}}),installationPreference:ae.subfield(et.z.enum(KA.MARKETPLACE_INSTALL_PREFS).optional(),{label:pe.msg({defaultMessage:"Installation",id:"47svuNMHCd"}),description:{short:ae.shortDescription(pe.msg({defaultMessage:"Whether users install plugins themselves or get them automatically.",id:"pMktInstD1"}),{docsOnly:!1}),long:ae.longDescription("`available` (the default) lets users install from the Directory's Organization tab. `auto_install` installs automatically once per pin (the commit SHA, or a `url` source's `manifestSha256`); a plugin the user removes stays removed until the pin changes. `required` reinstalls on every sync, so it cannot stay removed. An `auto_install` or `required` entry without that pin (a full 40-character commit SHA in `ref`, or `manifestSha256` for a `url` source) is treated as `available` and reported as a config warning: the marketplace still lists, but the entry installs nothing. Left at (or treated as) `available`, a `url` marketplace served from your inference gateway's or bootstrap server's own origin may instead mark individual plugins `\"installationPreference\": \"auto_install\"` in its `marketplace.json`: those install automatically with no pin (each such archive needs a `sha256`), and a plugin the user removes stays removed. On any other origin those marks are ignored.",{docsOnly:!1})}}),credentialKind:ae.subfield(et.z.enum(LA).optional(),FA),credentialHelper:ae.subfield(et.z.string().min(1).optional(),{label:pe.msg({defaultMessage:"Credential helper",id:"9bQZ2JN+mX"}),remotePolicy:{requiresUserConsent:!0},description:{short:ae.shortDescription(pe.msg({defaultMessage:"Executable that prints an access token for this marketplace.",id:"+x3hZrl+4b"}),{docsOnly:!1}),long:ae.longDescription("Prints to stdout one of: a bare token (sent as the git password for username `x-access-token`, which GitHub, GitLab and Azure DevOps accept, and as `Authorization: Bearer` for `url` sources); git-credential lines `username=<user>` and `password=<token>` when the host needs a particular username (Bitbucket Data Center project or repository access tokens on 9.3+: `x-token-auth`; GitLab deploy tokens: `gitlab+deploy-token-N`) \u2014 sent as HTTP Basic for `url` sources; or `authtype=Bearer` and `credential=<token>` to send `Authorization: Bearer <token>` (Bitbucket Data Center HTTP access tokens on any version). Other keys, blank lines and CRLF are ignored; JSON is not accepted.",{docsOnly:!1})},predicates:{show:MA,required:MA}})},xA={ref:ae.subfield(et.z.string().min(1).optional(),{label:pe.msg({defaultMessage:"Ref",id:"Yz6RnPXq2r"}),placeholder:pe.msg({defaultMessage:"Branch, tag, or commit SHA",id:"r5djcSLDYh"}),description:{short:ae.shortDescription(pe.msg({defaultMessage:"Commit SHA, branch, or tag. Leave empty to track the default branch; auto_install and required need a full 40-character commit SHA.",id:"pMktRefDs1"}),{docsOnly:!1})},predicates:{show:DA}}),path:ae.subfield(et.z.string().min(1).optional(),{label:pe.msg({defaultMessage:"Subpath",id:"Hy0W3kYc6J"}),description:{short:ae.shortDescription(pe.msg({defaultMessage:"Folder within the repository that contains the marketplace, when it isn\u2019t at the root.",id:"pMktPathD1"}),{docsOnly:!1})},predicates:{show:DA}}),...ZA},Ate={manifestSha256:ae.subfield(et.z.string().regex(lo.SHA256_HEX,"Manifest SHA-256 must be a 64-character hex digest").transform((e)=>e.toLowerCase()).optional(),{label:pe.msg({defaultMessage:"Manifest SHA-256",id:"pMktMfSha1"}),support:{availableInVersion:"1.32352.0"},placeholder:pe.msg({defaultMessage:"64-char hex SHA-256 of marketplace.json",id:"pMktMfSha2"}),description:{short:ae.shortDescription(pe.msg({defaultMessage:"SHA-256 of the exact marketplace.json to accept. Without it auto_install and required act as available; a served manifest with any other digest is refused.",id:"pMktMfSha3"}),{docsOnly:!1})},predicates:{show:$te}}),...ZA,credentialKind:ae.subfield(et.z.enum(KA.MARKETPLACE_CREDENTIAL_KINDS).optional(),FA)},L_={label:pe.msg({defaultMessage:"Source",id:"cc9hc4+0K4"}),support:{values:{url:{availableInVersion:"1.32352.0"}}},optionLabels:{github:pe.msg({defaultMessage:"GitHub",id:"SYEyDpPjNk"}),git:pe.msg({defaultMessage:"Git URL",id:"TpLDdW3nvS"}),url:pe.msg({defaultMessage:"Marketplace URL",id:"PjhC2D2FaO"})},description:{short:ae.shortDescription(pe.msg({defaultMessage:"Where the marketplace is fetched from: a GitHub repository (set repo), any Git remote (set url), or a hosted marketplace.json file (set url).",id:"l67dEmmDaG"}))},predicates:{required:()=>!0}},Tte=`For \`git\` sources, the HTTPS remote the app clones. For \`url\` sources, the HTTPS address of a \`marketplace.json\` whose plugins are \`archive\` entries (a zip \`url\` plus its \`sha256\`; \`ref\` and \`path\` do not apply). Archive URLs must be same-origin with the manifest URL: that origin is the only host to open on the firewall and the only one a credential is sent to. If any archive fails to download or verify, nothing from that fetch is installed and the next sync retries.

When Installation is \`auto_install\` or \`required\`, set \`manifestSha256\` to the SHA-256 of that exact file and give every archive a \`sha256\`: a served manifest with a different digest is refused and unpinned archives are skipped, so publishing a new manifest means updating \`manifestSha256\`; with no \`manifestSha256\` at all the entry is treated as \`available\` (and a config warning says so). A marketplace served from your inference gateway's or bootstrap server's own origin may instead leave Installation at \`available\` and mark individual plugins \`"installationPreference": "auto_install"\` in the manifest (each with a \`sha256\`); those install with no pin and a new manifest is picked up on the periodic re-fetch. On any other origin the per-plugin marks are ignored.

\`credentialKind\` selects what is sent: \`anonymous\` (the default) nothing, \`userGit\` the user's stored git credential for that host as HTTP Basic, \`credentialHelper\` the helper's output as \`Authorization\`, and \`inferenceCredential\` (\`url\` sources only) the credential the app already sends your inference gateway or enabled bootstrap server, so the manifest must be on one of those two origins; when there is nothing to send yet, no request is made and the entry reports why. See [Host the marketplace over HTTPS](${lo.COWORK_3P_DOCS_BASE}/extensions#host-the-marketplace-over-https-instead-of-git) for an example manifest and credential details.`,NA=ae.subfield(Fn.urlSchema({allowLoopbackHttp:!0}),{label:pe.msg({defaultMessage:"URL",id:"5M+YdqOWGS"}),isPrimaryKey:!0,description:{short:ae.shortDescription(pe.msg({defaultMessage:"HTTPS Git remote of the marketplace repository (git), or direct HTTPS URL of a hosted marketplace.json file (url).",id:"p6oo8hoZ4V"})),long:ae.longDescription(Tte)},predicates:{show:jA,required:jA}});KA.AllowedPluginMarketplace=et.z.discriminatedUnion("source",[et.z.object({source:ae.subfield(et.z.literal("github"),L_),repo:ae.subfield(et.z.string().regex(UA,"Repository must be in the form owner/repo, e.g. anthropics/skills").transform((e)=>e.toLowerCase()),{label:pe.msg({defaultMessage:"Repository",id:"ZHK3DVhcxt"}),isPrimaryKey:!0,placeholder:pe.msg({defaultMessage:"owner/repo",id:"3pZ8Ut7zIL"}),description:{short:ae.shortDescription(pe.msg({defaultMessage:"GitHub repository in owner/repo form. Case-insensitive.",id:"2cD0skIoWu"}))},predicates:{show:RA,required:RA}}),...xA}),et.z.object({source:ae.subfield(et.z.literal("git"),L_),url:NA,...xA}),et.z.object({source:ae.subfield(et.z.literal("url"),L_),url:NA,...Ate})]).refine((e)=>{var t;return((t=e.credentialKind)!==null&&t!==void 0?t:"anonymous")==="credentialHelper"===(e.credentialHelper!==void 0)},{message:"Credential helper is required when Auth is credentialHelper, and must be emp